    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d410">

                <pb facs="0627" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C111/890a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                            Diplomatic Officers in the American Republics
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-01">October 1,
                        1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: There is enclosed herewith a copy of the
                    message which, under date of September 27, 1935, I sent to the Chairman of the
                    Second <pb facs="0628" n="526" xml:id="pg526"/> Committee of the League Assembly
                    regarding the economic program adopted by that Committee.</p>
                <p>I desire you to furnish a copy of this message to the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs; in your covering note, you will please inform the Minister that I am
                    sure that he also will welcome the program adopted by the Committee as evidence
                    of the growing worldwide support for the fundamental principles embodied in the
                    agreements worked out at the Montevideo Conference.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d410-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d410-f1" n="6" xml:id="d410-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence concerning this Conference, see <ref target="frus1933v04#pg_1">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1933, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iv</hi>, pp. 1</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
